WEBVTT

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:10.210
Emi?

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:11.860
I think I'll leave after all...

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:13.150
Are you still talking about that?

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:15.650
No turning back since we're here already.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.340
Are you still hesitating there, Nozomi?

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:27.020
I'm sorry.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:34.770
Two months ago I got invited to this ghost-spotting event.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:39.550
That is where I met that person for the first time.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:50.650
Say, Takato-kun?

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:54.840
Do ghosts really come out at this spot?

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:56.190
Yeah.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:58.040
I'm sure the information is true.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:03.050
I've been told that a gang involved in a bank robbery got surrounded in this very same building.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:09.310
One of the gang members who feared he could not get away became desperate.

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:23.410
The fire expanded at a fast rate, which caused many innocent people to get caught in the fire.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:28.320
Not long after a strange rumour got spread.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:32.940
They say that a child who entered this building to play, not long after the incident, never returned.

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:36.790
And the same goes for the grown ups who went to search for that child in this building.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:43.580
And after that repeated itself, there was no one who still wanted to take on that case.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:44.740
And then one day people started to...

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:48.360
...call this place the man devouring building.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:51.820
Watch out.

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:56.040
I'm used to these kinds of places, but you guys might have to watch out.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:56.770
Yes.

00:03:56.930 --> 00:04:02.040
So this is the room where those bank robbers were, Takato?

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:02.630
Yeah.

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:04.610
Can't you feel it?

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:05.570
This immense strength.

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:07.380
Are you being serious?

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:08.470
Of course I am.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.860
You should go home already.

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:13.840
It's dangerous here.

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:16.410
Please wait, I would also...

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:24.520
A man...

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:26.000
What’s the matter?

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:29.310
A human body is lying over there.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:30.720
That can't be.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:32.700
There can’t be a real body here.

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:36.810
What is this?

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:38.320
It's just something made of paper-mâché.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:39.570
This must be a prank.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.020
Unbelievable.

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:44.470
It looks so much like a corpse.

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:47.000
But these are all real bills.

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:48.320
Impossible.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:50.000
Get away.

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:53.570
Get away from him immediately.

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:56.220
And who might you be?

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:57.910
Give it back.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:04:59.880
Give it back.

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:01.460
That's...

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:03.190
That's my money.

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:05.600
Give it back.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:06.770
Give it back!

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:13.070
What are you standing there for?

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:14.290
Get over here quickly!

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:16.360
Calm down!

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:18.740
If you continue that way, you'll get out of here!

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:21.830
How dare you take my money?!

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:23.680
I'm gonna kill you!

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:26.450
Hold on to me.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:29.910
Hurry up!

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:32.380
It's all my money!

00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:41.580
Please hold on.

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:42.200
Are you alright?

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:45.130
She’s dead.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.010
It can't...

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:51.100
I'll kill you and everyone else.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:57.360
You won't get away!

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:15.620
You're going to die!

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:30.290
The dead with a strong attachment to this world become Corpses.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:35.100
Living corpses rob the living from their lives.

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:37.510
I heard about you before.

00:06:37.510 --> 00:06:42.190
There is a group out there that tries to kill us by using Corpses like us.

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:44.530
You must be one of those Corpses!?

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:46.770
Damn!

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:49.240
You’re not human either!

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:52.500
If I had known that you weren't human, I wouldn't have gone easy on you.

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:59.490
That day a feeling, different from terror and astonishment, conquered my heart.

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:04.300
I thought that that person fighting was beautiful.

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:07.860
People may say that death is something scary.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:10.360
But is that really true?

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:14.680
Thanks to death, people can get liberated from this world.

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:16.400
Yes.

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:19.960
That person’s beauty was the beauty of death.

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:46.450
After that day I felt like I wanted to meet that person again.

00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:48.400
Note: Headline: "Best Places to Spot Ghosts"

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:49.850
After that day I felt like I wanted to meet that person again.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:52.320
I wonder why.

00:07:57.820 --> 00:08:04.650
But I never saw that person or a Corpse again.

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:17.270
She's there.

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:17.860
It's her.

00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:22.610
I thought I told you already.

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:25.250
Don't come near us anymore.

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:27.420
I know.

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:30.060
But there is something I want you to tell me.

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:31.180
Where is Minai?

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:33.350
Minai?

00:08:33.350 --> 00:08:33.850
Who’s that?

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:35.230
You know!

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:36.720
From the same Kougon-cult as you!

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:38.630
I don't know that person.

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:42.620
Did they kill her?

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:47.950
You really don't know anything?

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:50.200
We didn't do anything.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:52.070
But Keisei said the problem is solved.

00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:53.460
That's all I know.

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:54.910
Don't lie to me!

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:56.460
Minai...

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:57.680
Where did Minai go?!

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:05.750
Damn it.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:10.960
I feel like I saw him somewhere before.

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:12.610
Hey you.

00:09:13.730 --> 00:09:15.380
Are you one of Oori's friends?

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:17.620
No, I...

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:19.990
I'm sorry.

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:23.710
What a strange girl.

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:29.580
Say, Oori?

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:31.720
You must know something.

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:38.680
First I heard that a senpai had a strange death, and now I hear that another senpai stabbed someone.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:39.200
I...

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:41.970
I'm sorry.

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:45.630
Why are you guys looking so gloomy?

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:47.350
Why don't you two cheer up?

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:49.290
I wonder what will happen to the student council.
Why don't you two cheer up?

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:51.790
You’re the only one in the student council.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:54.130
I'm making you help out, aren't I?

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:58.450
At this year's roundup, you'll be drowning in work given by me, Inohiko Mizuki.

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:04.090
Next year, I'll be student president, and you as my workers, we'll reform this school!

00:10:04.090 --> 00:10:08.500
At the student council, we shall write this school's history.

00:10:09.070 --> 00:10:11.040
Listen to me when I speak!

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:14.270
I know there is a lot going on.

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:16.840
But today I'll get rid of both of your worries at once.

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:18.950
I'm gonna show you guys something big!

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:26.800
Isn't that Kasuka?

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:28.050
Is this it?

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:29.300
What do you mean by that?

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:32.600
Note: Omune-sama means something like sacred breasts.
That girl will become our Omune-sama.

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:33.720
Omune-sama?

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:37.410
Behold!

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:44.260
A perfect idol.

00:10:44.260 --> 00:10:45.520
A perfect student.

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:47.890
But I’m going to broaden her horizon.

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:51.980
She is the goddess I am watching over ever since the entrance ceremony.

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:53.820
I didn't stand a chance with the transfer student, Itsuki.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:54.910
Unbelievable.
I didn't stand a chance with the transfer student, Itsuki.

00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:56.850
What is going to happen to the student council?
I didn't stand a chance with the transfer student, Itsuki.

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:56.890
I didn't stand a chance with the transfer student, Itsuki.

00:10:57.180 --> 00:11:00.320
Throw away your sadness, I'll make you happy!

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:01.270
Oh no!

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:01.860
Run!

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:06.540
That boy.

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:08.820
Hey.

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:11.880
Did you talk to Oori-kun after that?

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:13.930
No, what about you, Itsuki?

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:15.610
Not at all.

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:17.980
I feel like he’s ignoring me.

00:11:18.770 --> 00:11:21.940
I heard they disposed of Minai at the auditor’s place.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:25.330
It's only normal that we had to kill her.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:30.010
But it's a good thing, if he won't come near us from now on.

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:32.050
I guess you're right.

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:39.110
I wonder what will happen to Hoshino Makina.

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:41.550
I think she won't go near him at all.

00:11:42.210 --> 00:11:45.930
He thinks that Makina-chan is his brother's girlfriend.

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:49.090
Are those two like that?

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:51.010
That can’t be.

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:55.030
But I don't know about Makina-chan's feelings.

00:11:57.370 --> 00:11:59.440
You know, because you are a Shikabane Hime.

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:01.550
I guess.

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:06.260
Oori...

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:08.570
Oori...

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:10.780
What's wrong, Ushi?

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:11.740
Euhm...

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:15.300
This is Kagami Oori, Omune-sama.

00:12:16.650 --> 00:12:18.030
Breasts?

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:22.780
I’m sorry to bother you like this.

00:12:22.780 --> 00:12:24.560
It’s okay, really.

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:28.810
Ushijima-kun told me he was a friend of you.

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:30.030
Well, I...

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:31.480
Kagami Oori-kun?

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:33.090
I’m going to be straightforward.

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:34.480
Yes?!

00:12:34.970 --> 00:12:36.880
You must give up that girl.

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:38.600
That girl?

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:41.700
The one you were waiting for in front of the temple.

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:43.570
A long haired beautiful girl.

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:47.530
She must be talking about that Shikabane Hime, Oori.

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:49.440
Hoshimura Makina?

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:50.890
Makina?

00:12:50.890 --> 00:12:52.930
So she’s called Hoshimura Makina?

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:54.190
That girl.

00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:55.240
Yeah.

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:58.210
But I think you shouldn't get to close to her.

00:12:58.970 --> 00:12:59.620
Why is that?

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:01.540
Why, you ask?

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:02.560
That’s because...

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:06.150
Shikabane Hime attracts those who long for death.

00:13:06.710 --> 00:13:09.380
Could this girl have seen death too?

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:11.650
Just like you have.

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:15.640
Are you all right?

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:17.130
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:13:18.050 --> 00:13:22.890
You attract Shikabane Hime, because you are drawn to death.

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:25.960
You can't run away from it anymore.

00:13:26.650 --> 00:13:27.210
Shut up!

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:37.490
It's not what it seems like.

00:13:37.490 --> 00:13:39.210
I tried to catch a cat.

00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:46.560
Liar!

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:48.600
There is no cat here!

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:50.310
But there really was one.

00:13:50.610 --> 00:13:53.710
You don't even know that girl's true identity.

00:13:53.710 --> 00:13:55.460
You're just following her around.

00:13:55.650 --> 00:13:56.410
You filthy bastard.

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:57.860
You call yourself a man.

00:13:57.860 --> 00:13:59.510
What do you mean by that?

00:13:59.510 --> 00:14:01.450
I was just warning you.

00:14:01.450 --> 00:14:05.010
I'll protect Makina-san from you.

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:12.430
No one can see me.

00:14:12.430 --> 00:14:14.430
Because I am you.

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:20.600
I finished it.

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:21.660
Here.

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:29.010
If you’re able to do this, your arm must be regenerated perfectly.

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:32.400
There are other ways to test that.

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:35.730
I'd made Oori help me, if he was here.

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:38.400
But it seems like he's quite angry at me.

00:14:39.880 --> 00:14:41.470
Who is Oori anyway?

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:45.030
You told me you found him.

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:48.260
It seems like the inspector Isaki knows something.

00:14:49.010 --> 00:14:50.330
What kind of child was he?

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.100
Just a normal child.

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:54.390
You’re wrong!

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:56.960
He was strange from the beginning.

00:14:56.960 --> 00:15:00.880
Even knowing my heart wasn't beating, that guy didn't get scared.

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:05.620
And the time with Minai, though he knew she was a Shikabane Hime.

00:15:05.620 --> 00:15:08.190
He treated her as a human being.

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:11.660
Why can he act that way?

00:15:12.020 --> 00:15:13.670
I don't think that's so normal.

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:20.820
He was around three years old, when he first came here.

00:15:23.590 --> 00:15:26.980
That time he didn't even know how to dress or even eat.

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:30.010
He didn't even know how to use the toilet.

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:34.460
And he knew nothing about human contact.

00:15:37.230 --> 00:15:38.480
One day...

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:43.690
Did you pick that up?

00:15:44.190 --> 00:15:45.240
No.

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:47.050
It was crying by the riverbank.

00:15:47.450 --> 00:15:49.290
That means you picked it up.

00:15:50.250 --> 00:15:52.850
You mean you didn't, right?

00:15:52.850 --> 00:15:54.110
It's your friend, right?

00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:59.080
Until then, Oori never showed any interest in other children.

00:15:59.210 --> 00:16:02.380
And the first time he cared about something, it was about a small living creature.

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:06.070
He knew nothing about taking care of it.

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:10.090
But it looked like Oori gradually started living.

00:16:11.510 --> 00:16:12.690
But then...

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:18.230
How cruel.

00:16:18.590 --> 00:16:20.310
Let's bury it.

00:16:20.310 --> 00:16:22.610
Riko, can you get gloves and some incense sticks?

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:24.330
I'll go get the shovel.

00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:29.470
When the cat that turned from a living thing into a just a thing, Oori just kept on staring.

00:16:35.960 --> 00:16:36.720
Oori?

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:45.160
Why did you bring it to such a place?

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:51.090
This is the place I met him, so this is the place I'll let him cry again.

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:57.060
Cry again!

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:06.280
Oori, the only thing we can do for the dead is remember their death and cry.

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:09.840
Priests aren't here for the dead.

00:17:10.600 --> 00:17:13.440
We're here for the living, drowning in sadness.

00:17:14.060 --> 00:17:17.360
So you must cry, Oori.

00:17:17.920 --> 00:17:18.780
Go on and cry.

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:31.460
I believe that that was Oori's first feeling.

00:17:32.910 --> 00:17:35.420
Usually people forget about death.

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:40.070
For example, if you think about death suddenly, you forget about it right away.

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:44.580
But Oori can't forget about death as easily as normal people.

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:47.050
He thinks it's something you can't forget.

00:17:47.610 --> 00:17:48.500
Why?

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:51.210
He'll only make himself feel bad.

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:53.020
It doesn't help himself at all.

00:17:53.020 --> 00:17:54.070
Anyway.

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:56.320
I'll be going now.

00:17:56.810 --> 00:17:57.570
Where to?

00:17:58.560 --> 00:18:01.000
I have to drop by the Honzan sometime anyway.

00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:18.960
Oori.

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:22.090
Did you forget...

00:18:25.220 --> 00:18:26.900
...about me already?

00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:30.230
You're alive?

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:33.000
Oori-kun, what’s the matter?

00:18:33.690 --> 00:18:34.610
The cat.

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:38.700
Stop crying and try to get some sleep.

00:18:39.490 --> 00:18:40.740
Good night.

00:18:43.780 --> 00:18:45.420
Why?

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:48.130
You are the only one who can see me.

00:18:48.130 --> 00:18:49.580
I am you.

00:18:50.430 --> 00:18:52.010
Did you already forget?

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:53.270
About me.

00:18:53.990 --> 00:18:55.380
About us!

00:18:57.550 --> 00:18:59.070
Not again.

00:18:59.690 --> 00:19:00.780
I'm sorry.

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:02.460
I was lost in my thoughts.

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:04.540
About that girl?

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:05.790
We're sorry about that.

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:09.050
No.

00:19:09.050 --> 00:19:14.160
She said she had to go somewhere no matter what, so we had to let her go.

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:16.170
You still don't know where she's at?

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:17.760
It’s alright.

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:20.460
I'm sorry to have bothered you with that.

00:19:26.920 --> 00:19:27.940
Excuse me.

00:19:29.030 --> 00:19:30.640
Are you Makina-san?

00:19:31.430 --> 00:19:32.590
Are you that girl from...

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:35.120
You saved me from the Man-eating building.

00:19:35.120 --> 00:19:37.000
I'm Kasuka Nozomi.

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:40.360
Thank you so much for that day.

00:19:42.770 --> 00:19:44.480
It's best for you to forget about that.

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:47.850
Not only about me, but also about that night.

00:19:47.850 --> 00:19:49.030
I can't forget about that.

00:19:49.030 --> 00:19:49.990
Makina-san!

00:19:50.550 --> 00:19:51.310
Go home.

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:53.610
Why?

00:19:53.610 --> 00:19:56.550
Oori doesn't understand anything about you.

00:19:57.800 --> 00:19:58.990
He's no good.

00:19:58.990 --> 00:20:01.000
That boy doesn't know anything.

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:03.070
Not about you or death.

00:20:03.530 --> 00:20:04.520
Death?

00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:08.840
Death is eternal, and is something only the chosen ones can approach.

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:10.520
The beauty of death...

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:13.360
That is the reason why I...

00:20:13.360 --> 00:20:14.480
Death is only death.

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:16.950
It is nothing else but that.

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:17.440
But...

00:20:17.870 --> 00:20:19.780
What do you know about Oori?

00:20:20.540 --> 00:20:24.100
Oori understands death much more then you.

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:26.610
About you too?

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:39.560
I'm sorry.

00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:45.000
Because of me, there seems to be some misunderstanding with that girl.

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:46.350
Don't worry about it.

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:49.280
I thought you weren't going to come here anymore.

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:53.860
That one is with you from time to time.

00:20:54.460 --> 00:20:56.470
Is it OK to keep pets at your apartment?

00:20:58.110 --> 00:20:59.530
You can see him?

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:02.760
No matter how dark it gets, I can see a little cat.

00:21:03.850 --> 00:21:05.690
If you're here for Keisei, he's at the Honzan.

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:08.890
Can I ask you something?

00:21:10.180 --> 00:21:11.300
About Minai?

00:21:13.240 --> 00:21:17.200
When I thought about it, I realized I know nothing about that girl.

00:21:17.990 --> 00:21:20.720
If you want, could you tell me what kind of girl she was?

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:26.920
The only thing we can do for the dead is remember them and cry.

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:29.720
My brother told me that a long time ago.

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:35.160
But I can't remember her that well, if I know nothing about her.

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:41.550
We only have tea.

00:21:44.220 --> 00:21:44.910
Thank you.

00:23:26.490 --> 00:23:30.970
Stars shine in the sky while people squirm and struggle with death below.

00:23:31.520 --> 00:23:35.780
But when the living and the dead switch places, people may betray their nature.

00:23:35.780 --> 00:23:39.260
And then even the stars on the ground begin to twinkle.
